# Line endings, and one of them is load-bearing.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, which
# rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout. That is harmless for Python and
# TypeScript and fatal for a shell script that runs as a container's
# entrypoint: a CR at the end of the shebang makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter literally called "/usr/bin/env sh\r", and the container exits
# with "no such file or directory" naming a file that is obviously there.
#
# So scripts and the container's own files are pinned to LF regardless of who
# checks them out. `backend/Dockerfile` strips CRs from `start.sh` at build
# time as well - belt and braces, because a build can start from a tarball that
# never went through git at all.

# Let git decide for ordinary source, and normalise it in the repository.
* text=auto

# Anything a Linux kernel or shell has to read. Never CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers, the other way round.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.riv binary
